From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:59:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 0/9] microblaze: fix the fortified longjmp hang, destructors and cancellation; add ucontext, CFI and a working backtrace

The MicroBlaze port has never had its testsuite run, and this series is
what fell out of running it (under qemu-user and, for the signal-frame
cases, qemu-system with a real kernel).  Patches apply to current master
with git am in this order: 1-5 are bug fixes, 6 is testsuite-only, 7-9
add functionality.  8 must follow 2 and 7 (start.S, setcontext.S), and 9
must follow 7 (the Linux Makefile).

Bugs:

  1/9  microblaze: Implement ____longjmp_chk using the generic Linux version
       The function has been a two-instruction stub (rtsd r15,0; nop) since
       the 2012 port, so every fortified longjmp/siglongjmp hangs.
  2/9  microblaze: Pass _dl_fini to __libc_start_main so destructors run
       _start passed 0; since 2.34 nothing else runs .fini_array in a
       dynamically linked program.
  3/9  microblaze: fix stack-argument offsets in __syscall_cancel_arch
       Arguments 5 and 6 were read from r1+56/60; the ABI puts them at
       r1+28/32.  pread64/pwrite64 through a cancellation point got a
       garbage offset (aio_suspend, nptl/tst-cancel17).
  4/9  microblaze: tail-call __syscall_do_cancel so -fexceptions
       cancellation unwinds
       brlid made an asm frame with no unwind info, so the forced unwind
       stopped there and cleanup handlers never ran.
  5/9  elf: Terminate the .eh_frame section of ld.so
       ld.so is linked without sofini.os; add an rtld flavour of it.  Not
       MicroBlaze-specific; happy to send it on its own if preferred.

Testsuite:

  6/9  microblaze: Tell the libm tests that soft-float has no exceptions or
       rounding modes (they abort before running otherwise).

Functionality:

  7/9  microblaze: Implement getcontext, setcontext, swapcontext and
       makecontext (they were the ENOSYS stubs).
  8/9  microblaze: Add CFI to the assembly sources
       Behind a configure probe: the assembler only accepts .cfi_* with the
       gas patch posted to binutils@ ("gas: Support CFI directives for
       MicroBlaze"); without it the macros expand to nothing and the build
       is unchanged.
  9/9  microblaze: Use the generic unwinder-based backtrace
       The port's own prologue-scanning backtrace misfires and stops early.

Full unwinding through a signal frame on glibc additionally needs a libgcc
fix (the upstream MD_FALLBACK_FRAME_STATE_FOR uses sizeof(ucontext_t),
which is 120 bytes larger under glibc than the kernel's); that is a
separate patch to gcc-patches and is not required by anything here.

Sam Price (1):
  microblaze: tail-call __syscall_do_cancel so -fexceptions cancellation
    unwinds

Samuel Price (8):
  microblaze: Implement ____longjmp_chk using the generic Linux version
  microblaze: Pass _dl_fini to __libc_start_main so destructors run
  microblaze: fix stack-argument offsets in __syscall_cancel_arch
  elf: Terminate the .eh_frame section of ld.so
  microblaze: Tell the libm tests that soft-float has no exceptions or
    rounding modes
  microblaze: Implement getcontext, setcontext, swapcontext and
    makecontext
  microblaze: Add CFI to the assembly sources
  microblaze: Use the generic unwinder-based backtrace

